Kevin Wayne <killedbyafoo@yahoo.com> wrote:
> But is displacement actually stronger than invisibility against
> monsters without see invisible? I've never gotten the impression that
> it was. I thought that the main advantage to displacement would be
> that it would cause missed hit attempts by monsters even if they did
> have see invisible.

Incorrect.  Displacement is an essentially stronger effect.

Roughly speaking:
When you're invisible, a monster has a 1/3 chance of 
automatically finding you, otherwise it'll guess up to 1 square away.
When you're displaced (and visible), a monster has a 1/4 chance of
automatically finding you, otherwise it'll guess up to 2 squares away.

So the chance of a monster managing to get the square where you are is
much less.  Also, it's significantly easier to evade monsters... with
displacement, they'll sometimes step directly away from you, which never
happens with invisibility.  Similarly, just today I was fighting an
elf-lord who zapped a wand of fire in the opposite direction from where
I was.  Lovely!

